# =============================================================================
# Jersey Addicts BD — Monorepo Environment
# Place at REPO ROOT. Loaded by @jab/web (Next), @jab/db (Prisma), @jab/server.
# Copy to .env and fill secrets. Never commit .env / .env.local.
# =============================================================================

# --- Runtime ---
NODE_ENV=development

# --- Apps ---
# @jab/web (Next.js App Router) — http://localhost:3000
APP_URL=http://localhost:3000
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000
NEXT_PUBLIC_USE_API=true
# Leave empty for same-origin /api (recommended in monorepo)
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=

# CORS (comma-separated). Local defaults are always allowed.
# On Vercel, VERCEL_URL / *.vercel.app are allowed automatically — still set this
# for any custom domain, e.g.:
# CORS_ORIGIN=https://classic-football-jerseys-web.vercel.app,https://yourdomain.com
CORS_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000,http://127.0.0.1:3000

# --- Auth (JWT for API) ---
AUTH_SECRET="replace-with-openssl-rand-base64-32"
AUTH_URL=http://localhost:3000

# --- Database (Neon PostgreSQL) — used by @jab/db ---
# Pooled (runtime / Prisma Client). On Vercel use the *pooler* host.
# Do NOT use channel_binding=require (hangs Node/Prisma on serverless).
# Recommended flags:
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@ep-xxxx-pooler.region.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require&pgbouncer=true&connect_timeout=15"
# Direct / unpooled (migrations only) — host WITHOUT "-pooler".
# REQUIRED on Vercel — missing this causes P1002 advisory-lock timeouts during build.
# Build scripts will try to strip "-pooler" automatically, but set this explicitly.
DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@ep-xxxx.region.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require"

# Do NOT set NODE_ENV in Vercel project env (leave unset; runtime sets production).

# --- Seed (@jab/db) ---
# Super admin login after seed: admin@epicvanskap.com
SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD="ChangeMeNow!"
SEED_CUSTOMER_PASSWORD="Customer123!"

# --- Optional standalone API (@jab/server via npm run dev:api) ---
API_PORT=4000

# --- Optional integrations ---
# BKASH_APP_KEY=
# BKASH_APP_SECRET=

# Cloudinary (REQUIRED for product / banner / media image uploads)
# Dashboard → Settings → API Keys → copy "API environment variable"
# Format: cloudinary://API_KEY:API_SECRET@CLOUD_NAME
CLOUDINARY_URL=
# Or set separately instead of CLOUDINARY_URL:
# CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=
# CLOUDINARY_API_KEY=
# CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET=

# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=

# --- Vercel ---
# Build: npm run vercel-build (generate → migrate → next build)
# Framework: Next.js. Output Directory: dist (next.config distDir on VERCEL).
# Root Directory: apps/web (recommended for this repo) OR repository root.
# Node.js: 24.x (engines in package.json)
# Required env: DATABASE_URL, DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED (or only DATABASE_URL — build falls back),
# AUTH_SECRET, CORS_ORIGIN, NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL, NEXT_PUBLIC_USE_API
#
# If build fails with P1001 (Can't reach database) OR missing DATABASE_URL:
#   1. Neon console → Resume compute if suspended (free tier auto-sleeps)
#   2. Confirm DATABASE_URL (pooler) + DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED (no -pooler) on Vercel
#      for Production AND Preview (GitHub PR / branch deploys need Preview too)
#   3. Re-deploy — build retries with wake delays; continues without migrate by default
#   4. Optional: SKIP_DB_MIGRATE=1 to skip migrate (only if schema is already current)
#   5. Optional: ALLOW_BUILD_WITHOUT_MIGRATE=0 to fail the build hard on missing DB / P1001
